## Task

You are proving a trigonometric equality one step at a time.
A proof strategy has already been provided. Follow it.

Write exactly ONE new step as a YAML code block. Do not repeat previous steps.
The last step of the complete proof must state the target equality.

## Step format

```yaml
<step_id>:
  - ["<lhs>", "<rhs>"]
  - <justification>
```

Justifications can be:
- `{rule: <rule_name>, vars: {<var>: "<value>", ...}}` — apply a rewriting rule
- `{step: <prev_step_id>}` — substitute a previously obtained equality
- `{sym: <prev_step_id>}` — flip lhs and rhs of a previous step
- `{trans: [<step_id_1>, ..., <step_id_n>]}` — chain steps transitively

All expressions must use Python syntax (parsable by `sympy.sympify`). Exponentiation is `**`.

## Available rules

```
{% for rule, (lhs, rhs) in globals.rules.items() %}
- {{ rule }}: `{{ lhs }} = {{ rhs }}`
{% endfor %}
```
